"There's an old saying every smith knows. That in those days the kingdom had a smith no one could match at smelting. That he alone could work what others couldn't even melt. That on the eve of the Ashen Sun, that smith shut a handful of fire inside that nameless metal. And that he carved his own name nowhere on the spear. My family is a side branch that borrowed embers from that man's hearth.",
"▷ Why didn't he carve his own name?",
"For fear the fire would swallow that name first. It was a fire that had swallowed nothing yet, and the first thing it swallowed must not be its maker's name. That is why no one knows that smith's name. Only that no one could match him. He too served under the King of the Hearth, and they say the king locked the doors with the smiths still in the forge.",
"Only the fire he shut away came out. They say the spear chooses. In a hand that means to command the fire it is only a heavy spear, and it shines only in a hand that has accepted the fire. It shines in yours. The tale of the locked forge can wait until you see the place yourself.",
