"Getting started",
"The surveyor's tools",
"A surveyor has a few tools. All are used by holding them and right-clicking.\n\n· Surveyor's Codex: records the mobs you met, the mobs you slew and the gear you obtained.\n· Surveyor's Guidebook: the book you are reading now.\n· Survey Compass: shows the direction and distance of the place your current quest is looking for.\n· Return Ticket: takes you back to town. (See the 'Return tickets' page.)\n· Weapon Manual: you receive one the first time you obtain a weapon with a special skill.\n\nYou receive one Codex and one Guidebook at the start. If you lose them, the general store sells them again.",
"codex guidebook compass manual tools",
"Talking to NPCs",
"Right-click a townsperson to open the dialogue box.\n\n· The top choice is that person's own work (shop, bank, jobs, attendance, gacha…).\n· A story marked '✦' is one you have not heard yet.\n· [Quests] shows the quests you can take and the ones in progress.\n· [Talk history] lets you reread what has been said so far.\n\nChat with the same person long enough and now and then they let slip something you cannot hear anywhere else.",
"talk dialogue choices stories",
"Quests and the journal",
"Quests are taken in conversation with NPCs. Fill the goals, go back, and you receive the reward.\n\n· Quest journal: /rtshop quest (you can bind a key in the controls)\n· You can have 10 in progress at once, and an abandoned quest can be taken again.\n· The quest display on screen shows each goal's progress and whom to visit.\n· Only one combat job quest line and one life job quest line can be in progress at a time.",
